# Component-level software metadata; root CITATION.cff continues to cite PMx Explain.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "When using the MultiOmics analysis software, cite this component metadata and the exact archived release once available."
type: software
title: "MultiOmics: guided single- and multi-omics analysis with explicit scientific validity checks"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic research-software component of PMx Explain. Guided single-omic
  and multiblock interfaces, input/design checks, reference R method adapters,
  and reproducible methodological reporting. This component is not a
  clinical decision support device and does not certify nominal statistical
  false discovery control for an arbitrary study.
authors:
  - family-names: Berrah
    given-names: Racym
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6432-2880"
    affiliation: "UMR 1248 Pharmacologie et Transplantation, Inserm, Université de Limoges, CHU de Limoges"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rberrah/rberrah.github.io"
url: "https://rberrah.github.io/pharmacometrie/multiomics/"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - multi-omics
  - single-omics
  - reproducible research software
  - statistical validation
# No version, DOI or release date is asserted until a frozen release exists.
